+## Subtopics
+
+### Flat Normals
+A technique to return flat vertex normals in worldspace for voxel terrains and Nanite static meshes [S2]. It uses the Voxel Flat Normal node in materials and requires disabling Tangent Space Normals in the material settings [S2]. On non-Nanite static meshes, the node returns standard vertex normals instead of flat normals [S2]. Flat normals cause significant seams when using Nanite Tessellation [S2].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ for a single cube, as the number of vertices and normals is fixed.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ for a single cube. Each cube requires 24 normals × 3 floats × 4 bytes = 288 bytes for normals, plus 288 bytes for positions (assuming float32).
-*   **Measured Performance:** Not given in the sources.
-*   **Strengths:** Simple to implement; produces correct flat shading for voxel geometry; preserves sharp edges.
-*   **Limitations:** Only suitable for axis-aligned cubes; does not support smooth shading or curved surfaces.
